.Dd November 17, 2026
.Dt PUB5-ADMIN 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm pub5-admin
.Nd fixed-verb privileged broker for pub5 production operations
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar verb arguments ...
.Nm
.Cm deploy-run-write
.Ar run-id
.Ar JSON
.Nm
.Cm deploy-run-read
.Ar run-id
.Nm
.Cm deploy-run-list
.Nm
.Cm deploy-run-pending-list
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the root-owned broker installed at
.Pa /usr/local/sbin/pub5-admin .
It exposes a bounded argv protocol for selected service, resource, application
layout, deployment and CI operations.
It does not evaluate shell command
strings and does not accept an arbitrary filesystem path as a command selector.
.Pp
The
.Cm deploy-run-write ,
.Cm deploy-run-read ,
.Cm deploy-run-list
and
.Cm deploy-run-pending-list
verbs manage fleet-level deploy receipts below
.Pa /var/db/pub5/deploy_runs .
The directory is root-owned and mode 0700; receipt files are root-owned and mode
0600. Writes validate the fixed schema and replace each receipt atomically.
The receipt binds one run ID to its target, owner process identity, pinned and
previous commit SHAs, original running-service snapshot, app ports, restore order,
log paths and most recent stage. Once the snapshot is recorded, its service set,
ports, restore order and SHAs cannot be changed.
.Pp
.Cm deploy-run-pending-list
is the bounded monitoring view. It returns up to 500 newest matching receipt
files and at most 100 pending records in a JSON object containing
.Cm pending ,
.Cm scanned ,
.Cm returned
and
.Cm truncated .
A true
.Cm truncated
value means the monitor did not inspect the complete receipt history; an empty
.Cm pending
array in that response is not proof that no older pending receipt exists.
The full
.Cm deploy-run-list
verb remains available to the explicit operator recovery plan.
.Pp
The broker requires effective root privileges through the reviewed
.Xr doas 1
path.
The deploy script checks that the installed broker exists, is executable,
and is not a symbolic link before continuing.
.Pp
Unknown verbs, unapproved services, invalid argument shapes and paths outside
the explicit allowlist are refused.
The broker is an internal privilege
boundary, not a general-purpose shell.
.Pp
Do not write deploy receipts directly from the deploy shell or alter their
snapshot fields. Use only the fixed deploy-run verbs. Recovery is operator-driven
through
.Xr vps-deploy 8 ;
the broker does not start, stop or restart services for a receipt.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
doas /usr/local/sbin/pub5-admin service check relayd
doas /usr/local/sbin/pub5-admin disk-usage /home
.Ed
.Sh SECURITY
Do not expand the verb set or replace fixed argv validation with shell
evaluation.
Update the calling contract and its regression tests when the
privileged interface changes.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr doas 1 ,
.Xr rcctl 8 ,
.Xr vps-deploy 8
